12. REVIEW ATTACK COOLDOWNS WITHOUT BREAKING COMBAT

Alva has an intentional cooldown policy:

* Ordinary repeated moves: historically 0.5 seconds.
* Exceptional effects: historically 3 seconds.
* High-impact 10-damage moves: historically 5 seconds.

Preserve the existence of meaningful cooldown categories.

However, investigate whether the ordinary repeat delay disproportionately slows basic combat.

Do not mistake the repeat cooldown for the duration of every attack.

These are different systems.

Evaluate whether quick attacks would benefit from a more responsive repeat policy, for example an experimental ordinary repeat delay between 0.3 and 0.5 seconds.

Consider whether the best solution is actually improved move diversity and follow-up flow rather than reduced cooldowns.

If changing the policy:

* Change it centrally.
* Update every dependent system.
* Preserve exceptional cooldown intent.
* Test against repeated attack exploitation.
* Check CPU behaviour.
* Update the product specification and tests.
* Do not weaken cooldown enforcement only for the human player.

Avoid introducing infinite offensive loops.

