13.2 Game controllers

Check:

* Left-stick steering.
* Dead zones.
* Dash direction selection.
* Direction changes during attacks.
* Jump presses during recovery.
* Input buffering.
* Button mapping interactions.
* Diagonal movement handling where relevant.

Avoid dead zones that make steering feel delayed.

Avoid overly sensitive dead zones that cause unintended movement.

Respect customized controller profiles.

13.3 Mobile touch controls

Alva supports touchscreen layouts.

Ensure all implemented mechanics remain accessible using the existing touch schemes, or update those schemes deliberately.

Check:

* Simultaneous movement and attack inputs.
* Touch release behaviour.
* Joystick direction changes.
* Jump and fast fall.
* Dash requests.
* Input timing under variable rendering performance.
* Responsive hit targets.
* Multi-touch interactions.

Do not require complex input combinations that are impractical on a phone.

13.4 Device parity

Equivalent gameplay inputs should produce equivalent gameplay results.

Differences in the physical interface are fine.

Differences in fighter physics or action privileges are not, unless explicitly part of an accessibility feature.

